(Bug #45 — the other right column, and the one that surprised the fix. An
 argument is NOT an untyped position: the callee's parameter declares its own
 type, and that is what the result is read as. `'opaque label'` handed to a
 `text` parameter has always printed "hi", so the rejection deliberately does
 not reach here.)

To 'opaque label'. Return "hi".

To 'announce label' with a text called label.
  print label.

'announce label' with 'opaque label'.
